ussions":false,"forks_count":1201,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":7608,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["cloud-native","cpp","database","distributed-database","distributed-sql","distributed-sql-database","high-performance","kubernetes","multi-cloud","multi-region","scale-out","sql"],"visibility":"public","forks":1201,"open_issues":7608,"watchers":9958,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"A few bugs must be fixed before the beta tag can be removed for SPLIT AT feature.  The following report is an example of a scanning error.\r\n\r\nWhen running the following valid statements, server erroneously reports an error on index scan on partial index.\r\n```sql\r\nCREATE TABLE rn (i int, j int, PRIMARY KEY (i ASC)) SPLIT AT VALUES ((3), (5));\r\nINSERT INTO rn VALUES\r\n    (1, 10),\r\n    (2, 20),\r\n    (3, 30),\r\n    (4, 40),\r\n    (5, 50),\r\n    (6, 60);\r\nCREATE INDEX ON rn (j ASC) WHERE j < 40;\r\nSELECT * FROM rn WHERE j < 50; -- foreign scan: works fine\r\nSELECT j FROM rn WHERE j < 40; -- index only scan: works fine\r\nSELECT * FROM rn WHERE j < 40; -- index scan: fails\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\nERROR:  Query error: Given ybctid is not associated with any row in table: 0 vs. 1\r\n```\r\n\r\nI haven't experimented much with other cases.  This was tested on CentOS GCC debug build on commit 8ab79a251af59fcd559dbfa612da1ece3fe2fb72.\r\n\r\nRelated: #3833\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/4770/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/4770/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/720943255","html_url":"https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/3833#issuecomment-720943255","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/3833","id":720943255,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDcyMDk0MzI1NQ==","user":{"login":"jaki","id":16715704,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NzE1NzA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16715704?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki","html_url":"https://github.com/jaki","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaki/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-11-03T07:05:01Z","updated_at":"2020-11-03T07:05:01Z","body":"I got something like this again.  Haven't been able to reproduce the issue, yet, but the way I got it was\r\n\r\n1. Do test in issue #6097\r\n1. Add more indexes so that you get\r\n\r\n   ```sql\r\n   \\d tablename\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n   ```\r\n                Table \"public.tablename\"\r\n    Column |  Type   | Collation | Nullable | Default\r\n   --------+---------+-----------+----------+---------\r\n    p      | integer |           | not null |\r\n    i1     | integer |           |          |\r\n    i2     | integer |           |          |\r\n    n      | integer |           |          |\r\n    t      | text    |           |          |\r\n   Indexes:\r\n       \"tablename_pkey\" PRIMARY KEY, lsm (p)\r\n       \"tablename_i1_i2_idx\" lsm (i1 HASH, i2)\r\n       \"tablename_i1_i2_idx1\" lsm ((i1, i2) HASH)\r\n       \"tablename_i1_i2_idx2\" lsm (i1 DESC, i2 DESC)\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n   The scans from here on will prioritize using the last index.\r\n\r\n1. Verify things work when doing point selects\r\n\r\n   ```sql\r\n   do $$\r\n   declare\r\n      a int := 0;\r\n      b int := 0;\r\n   begin\r\n      for counter in 0..100000 loop\r\n         select count(*) from tablename where i1 = counter and i1 = i2 into a;\r\n         b := a + b;\r\n      end loop;\r\n      raise notice 'value: %', b;\r\n   end; $$;\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n   ```\r\n   NOTICE:  value: 100000\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n1. Get the error when doing order by select\r\n\r\n   ```sql\r\n   BEGIN ISOLATION LEVEL SERIALIZABLE, READ ONLY, DEFERRABLE;\r\n   with w as (select * from tablename order by i1 desc, i2 desc) select count(*) from w;\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n   ```\r\n   ERROR:  Query error: Given ybctid is not associated with any row in table\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n   Stack trace:\r\n\r\n   ```\r\n   0x7f98f6b9ed2d  YBCGetStackTrace (src/yb/common/ybc_util.cc:287)\r\n    @           0x9b22c5  errmsg (src/postgres/src/backend/utils/error/elog.c:867)\r\n    @           0x9d9315  HandleYBStatusAtErrorLevel (src/postgres/src/backend/utils/misc/pg_yb_utils.c:325)\r\n    @           0x9d9346  HandleYBStatus (src/postgres/src/backend/utils/misc/pg_yb_utils.c:309)\r\n    @           0x9d93af  HandleYBStatusWithOwner (src/postgres/src/backend/utils/misc/pg_yb_utils.c:362)\r\n    @           0x564ab3  ybcFetchNextHeapTuple (src/postgres/src/backend/access/ybc/ybcam.c:276)\r\n    @           0x564ab3  ybc_getnext_heaptuple (src/postgres/src/backend/access/ybc/ybcam.c:1269)\r\n    @           0x565d30  ybcingettuple (src/postgres/src/backend/access/ybc/ybcin.c:340)\r\n    @           0x4ff819  index_getnext_tid (src/postgres/src/backend/access/index/indexam.c:592)\r\n    @           0x4ffae2  index_getnext (src/post