Select (src/postgres/src/backend/tcop/pquery.c:943)\r\n    @           0x8709ff  PortalRun (src/postgres/src/backend/tcop/pquery.c:784)\r\n    @           0x86a5b7  exec_simple_query (src/postgres/src/backend/tcop/postgres.c:1161)\r\n    @           0x86a5b7  yb_exec_simple_query (src/postgres/src/backend/tcop/postgres.c:4313)\r\n    @           0x86ce74  PostgresMain (src/postgres/src/backend/tcop/postgres.c:4924)\r\n    @           0x7d92cc  BackendRun (src/postgres/src/backend/postmaster/postmaster.c:4428)\r\n    @           0x7d92cc  BackendStartup (src/postgres/src/backend/postmaster/postmaster.c:4094)\r\n    @           0x7d92cc  ServerLoop (src/postgres/src/backend/postmaster/postmaster.c:1737)\r\n    @           0x7d92cc  PostmasterMain (src/postgres/src/backend/postmaster/postmaster.c:1400)\r\n    @           0x72f66e  PostgresServerProcessMain (src/postgres/src/backend/main/main.c:234)\r\n    @           0x72f70a\r\n    @     0x7f98f5efd824  __libc_start_main (csu/libc-start.c:289)\r\n    @           0x492b88  (unknown) (sysdeps/x86_64/start.S:118)\r\n    @ 0xffffffffffffffff\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n   Trying the query again (after aborting the last transaction) results in the same error.  Trying the slightly different query\r\n\r\n   ```sql\r\n   BEGIN ISOLATION LEVEL SERIALIZABLE, READ ONLY, DEFERRABLE;\r\n   with w as (select 1 from tablename order by i1 desc, i2 desc) select count(*) from w;\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n   gives the desired 100000 result.\r\n\r\nRepeating _all_ the steps again with a different table name, I do not see the same \"ybctid\" error and get the desired 100000 result.  I have these two tables right now, and stopping/starting the cluster gives me the same results.  Since they take up disk space, I won't keep them for long, so let me know if you want to do some debugging on them.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/720943255/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1